// Twin of input/regression/part-combine-mmrest-after-apart-silence.ly.
// texidoc: "Normal rests are preferred over multi-measure rests. A multi-measure rest
// beginning in one part in the middle of a multi-measure rest in the other part appears
// as expected."
//
// The book is its own control: the two staves are the SAME pair of parts in the opposite
// order, so whatever the rule is, it has to come out identical on both.
//
// What LP does with it (measured, audit/lpreg/pcmmas.log):
//   bar 1  r2 vs R1*2 -> silence1/2: the ORDINARY rests are engraved, in the shared voice
//                        (dir unset, position 0), and the multi-measure rest goes to null
//   bar 2  R1 vs (still inside R1*2) -> one MultiMeasureRest, measure-count 1, position 0
//   both staves identical, ink for ink.
octave absolute
time 4/4

part sa1 { clef treble }
part sa2 { clef treble }
part sb1 { clef treble }
part sb2 { clef treble }

section A {
  sa1 { r2 r2 | R1 | }
  sa2 { R1*2 | }
  sb1 { R1*2 | }
  sb2 { r2 r2 | R1 | }
}

form main { ~A }

score main { combinedStaff { sa1 sa2 } combinedStaff { sb1 sb2 } }
